## TL;DR: East West Emerald Cut Diamond Ring

An emerald cut diamond ring east west setting rotates the stone 90 degrees — the long axis runs side-to-side across the finger instead of pointing toward the knuckle. Settings start at [$995](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-solitaire-in-14k-rose-gold-item-193756?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Total ring from $1,490 with a lab emerald cut, or $4,050 natural.

**12 settings across 3 styles:**
- **East West Solitaire:** [$995–$1,475](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=east-west&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — RG, WG, YG, Platinum
- **East West Diamond Engagement Ring:** [$1,635–$2,600](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=east-west&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — WG, YG, RG, Platinum
- **East West Sidestone & Pavé (1/4 ct tw):** [$1,840–$2,485](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=east-west&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — WG, YG, RG, Platinum

**3 named concepts:**
- **The 90-Degree Rule** — what changes (and what doesn't) when you rotate the stone
- **The Setting Floor** — why 1ct is the minimum for east-west orientation to work
- **The Width Advantage** — why the emerald cut is the best shape for east-west settings

