## East West Solitaire Settings: $995 to $1,475

The East West Solitaire is the purest expression of the east-west concept. Four prongs grip the emerald cut stone in horizontal orientation on a simple polished band. Nothing competes with the rotated stone — the entire ring is about that horizontal rectangle.

[![East west emerald cut diamond ring in yellow gold solitaire setting](/images/east-west-emerald-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=east-west&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

**East West Solitaire in 14k Rose Gold — [$995](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-solitaire-in-14k-rose-gold-item-193756?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (7 reviews)

The most affordable east-west setting in this lineup. Rose gold creates a warm, modern contrast against the architectural step-cut geometry of the emerald cut. The pink warmth of rose gold works especially well with the horizontal stone — the warm band frames the cool clarity of the step-cut table.

For a 1ct H-color stone, rose gold's warmth makes H-color look near-identical to G.

**East West Solitaire in 14k White Gold — [$1,050](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-solitaire-in-14k-white-gold-item-193754?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (7 reviews)

White gold is the most neutral choice for east-west settings. The silver-white metal lets the step-cut facets of the emerald cut dominate visually — no warmth competing with the stone's hall-of-mirrors effect. For buyers choosing VS1 clarity or higher, white gold maximizes the clean, clear appearance of the step-cut table.

**East West Solitaire in 14k Yellow Gold — [$1,050](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-solitaire-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-193755?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (7 reviews)

Yellow gold gives the east-west emerald cut its most vintage-influenced look. The horizontal stone in yellow gold recalls antique signet ring design — a stone lying flat and wide across the band, framed by warm gold. H-color stones [look excellent in yellow gold settings](/emerald-cut-diamond-ring-yellow-gold), saving on color grade without visible sacrifice.

**East West Solitaire in Platinum — [$1,475](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-solitaire-in-platinum-item-193753?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** (7 reviews)

Platinum's durability argument is stronger for east-west settings than for any other orientation. The horizontal prong placement means the prongs at the long ends of the stone receive lateral force from everyday knocks that north-south prongs don't face. Platinum is denser and more durable than white gold — the prongs maintain grip over years of daily wear where white gold prongs may flex.

Buyers who wear the ring daily should consider platinum for any east-west setting.

