## Stone Selection for East West Emerald Cut Rings

The stone for an east-west emerald cut ring uses identical proportion targets to any other emerald cut. L:W 1.30–1.50, depth 60–64%, table 61–69%. But east-west orientation amplifies two specific qualities: face-up length (because the stone's length now spans horizontally across the finger) and clarity (because the open step-cut table is always visible from above).

**Carat weight — apply The Setting Floor:** Minimum 1ct for east-west orientation. At 1ct, the stone measures approximately 6.5mm × 4.5mm. In east-west orientation, that 6.5mm spans visibly across the finger. At 1.5ct (7.5mm × 5.5mm), the horizontal span becomes emphatic.

**L:W ratio — go longer for east-west:** If you're choosing east-west specifically for the horizontal width effect, favor 1.40:1–1.50:1 over 1.30:1. The longer ratio creates a more pronounced horizontal bar. A 1.30:1 stone in east-west position looks nearly square from the wearer's perspective — the short dimension faces up and the long dimension runs sideways. A 1.45:1 stone creates a clearly elongated horizontal rectangle.

**Clarity — VS2 minimum, VS1 recommended:** The east-west orientation doesn't change the step-cut clarity rule. The open table shows inclusions in the emerald cut regardless of which direction the stone faces. VS2 is the absolute minimum. VS1 is the safe recommendation. Watch the stone video before buying any SI1 emerald cut — what passes in a round brilliant will often be visible in a step-cut.

**Color — G minimum in white/platinum, H in yellow/rose gold:** Color recommendations for east-west emerald cuts are identical to any emerald cut. The 90-degree rotation doesn't change how the step-cut facets reflect color. G in white gold or platinum. H in yellow or rose gold.

**Natural 1ct search:** [Browse GIA-certified 1ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — filter depth 60–64%, table 61–69%, VS2+ clarity, G+ color.

**Lab 1.5ct search:** [Browse IGI-certified 1.5ct lab emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/lab-grown-diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=1.4&caratMax=1.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — same proportion filters. Lab pricing makes 1.5ct accessible at the cost of a 1ct natural, and 1.5ct creates more dramatic east-west coverage.

