**Buyers wanting a distinctive ring:** The east-west orientation is still uncommon enough in engagement rings that it reads as a deliberate design statement. A [1ct GIA G-VS2](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in the [East West Diamond Ring in WG](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-193950?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at ~$4,635 total is the clearest expression of the modern east-west aesthetic.

